// # MCP CLI Command Interface — Anchor for Agents
//
// Logline: Front door for the mcp command surface. Re-exports the standalone server entry plus the safe-merge utility.
//
// Setup: The mcp binary has 2 subcommands: `mcp` (start the server) and `mcp-merge <file>` (idempotently inject the ooda entry into an agent-tool JSON config). The dispatch is a one-line argv match.
//
// Beats:
//   1. cmd_mcp.oo has run_ooda_mcp: parses --stdio/--file/--socket/--help, runs engine_server_run.
//   2. safe_merge.oo has run_ooda_mcp_merge: idempotent agent-config writer.
//   3. safe_merge_core.oo provides the pure string utilities used by safe_merge.
//   4. main.oo is the package's binary entry: parse argv[0] (the subcommand), dispatch, return Result<Int, String>.
//
// Note: the original cli/mcp/test.oo (which ran the 55/55 MCP test suite via ooda/qa/tests_llms/test_all.oo) was deleted. The mcp-test command will be re-added in a later phase when a self-contained test runner is in place.

import "cmd_mcp.oo";
import "safe_merge.oo";
import "safe_merge_core.oo";
